<p>A Russian drone strike hit a market in Nikopol, in Ukraine&#x27;s Dnipropetrovsk region, on Saturday morning, killing five people and injuring at least 19 others as civilians gathered in a busy market area. The attack turned an ordinary shopping period into another deadly reminder of the war&#x27;s toll on civilian life. The casualty toll varied slightly across reports. BBC and RBC said 21 and 19 people were injured, respectively, while The Straits Times reported 25 wounded, including a 14-year-old girl in critical condition. All three sources, however, said five people were killed, underscoring the continued danger facing residents in Ukrainian communities affected by the war.</p><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cp869m2gzr0o'>Russian attack on Ukraine market kills five</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/russian-strike-on-market-in-ukraine-kills-five-wounds-25'>Russian strike on market in Ukraine kills five, wounds 25</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://newsukraine.rbc.ua/news/t-rkiye-steps-in-to-host-next-round-of-ukraine-1775328416.html'>Five people are killed and 19 others are injured in a Russian drone strike on a market in Nikopol, Dnipropetrovsk Oblast, Ukraine.</a> - rbc.ua</li></ul>